# The runtime and the generated code agree on object layouts and virtual table
# slots by convention, and a disagreement is a silent miscompile. So the
# runtime carries a stamp, `__catmint_abi_N`, and every program refers to it:
# a runtime from a compiler with another N fails to link. The .check builds
# such a runtime and makes sure it is refused.

class Main from IO
  def main:
    out("stamped\n")
  end
end
